WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:05.250
All right, so Joe Biden did an event yesterday
where he spoke about Donald Trump's nomination

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:09.240
of Amy CONI Barrett to the Supreme Court to
replace Ruth Bader Ginsburg.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:14.719
We already looked at clips from the nomination
ceremony on Saturday that Donald Trump held

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:15.900
at the White House.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.470
And at this event, Joe Biden also took questions
from the media.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:24.990
Now, as all of you know, I don't agree with
Joe Biden on every policy or nearly every

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:25.990
policy.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:29.689
But in some places, I think Joe Biden has
put together some pretty reasonable platforms,

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:32.860
which I would love to see made a reality if
he becomes president.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:38.830
But Joe Biden yesterday did something really
well, which is that he refused to play Donald

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:44.040
Trump's games and he refused to play some
of the games that the media gets Donald Trump

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.040
to play.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.030
But Joe Biden wasn't going to go for it because
Joe Biden was asked in light of Trump's Supreme

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:56.140
Court nominee and the nomination being so
hypocritical, given that Republicans in 2016

00:00:56.140 --> 00:01:00.330
said, oh, we don't confirm justices in the
last year of a term.

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:05.030
And now with 40 days to go, they want to confirm
a Supreme Court justice.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:09.760
In light of that hypocrisy, a question that
has come up is whether Joe Biden will try

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:12.400
to pack the Supreme Court if he wins.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.990
Should Democrats try to pack the Supreme Court
now packing?

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:19.250
The Supreme Court is essentially expanding
the court.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:20.510
You add justices.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:26.130
So if Donald Trump gets Amy CONI Barrett confirmed,
you would have a Supreme Court that leans

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:30.229
six to three in the direction of conservatives.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:34.780
Joe Biden could add four seats to the Supreme
Court.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.510
That would make it a 13 justice court instead
of nine.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:44.290
And he could appoint left wing justices to
those four new seats, taking control of the

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.620
court back, making it a seven six Liberal
majority.

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:50.659
Now, of course, this is hugely controversial.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:52.230
It's a major issue.

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.710
It is a nonstarter.

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:59.780
If Joe Biden doesn't win and it doesn't happen
in conjunction with Democrats taking the Senate.

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:07.430
But the great thing Joe Biden does is he realizes
that whether he says yes or no, it's trouble

00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:10.519
and he's not going to play the game with the
reporter.

00:02:10.519 --> 00:02:12.980
And he keeps the focus on the now.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:21.239
Take a look at how Joe Biden handled this
piece.

00:02:21.239 --> 00:02:25.819
Almost no, I have no comment.

00:02:25.819 --> 00:02:30.049
This question Sanders is.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:43.819
Well, having worked as a person under any
circumstances, I am not.

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:49.209
And I know you're going to be upset with my
answer, but what I'm not going to do is play

00:02:49.209 --> 00:02:54.340
the Trump game, which is a good game he plays.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.690
Take your eye off the issue before us.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:02.309
If I were to say yes or no to that, that becomes
a big issue.

00:03:02.309 --> 00:03:04.269
That's the headline here.

00:03:04.269 --> 00:03:07.840
I am focused on one thing right now, and I
really mean it.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:13.709
I'm focused on making sure the American people
understand that they're being cut out of this

00:03:13.709 --> 00:03:14.709
process.

00:03:14.709 --> 00:03:21.551
They're entitled to be part of the cut out
designed in order to take away the ACA and

00:03:21.551 --> 00:03:24.879
your health care in the midst of a pandemic.

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:26.189
That's the focus.

00:03:26.189 --> 00:03:27.189
That's what it's on.

00:03:27.189 --> 00:03:28.230
And that's the deal.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.819
Thank you also very, very much.

00:03:29.819 --> 00:03:31.019
Thank you.

00:03:31.019 --> 00:03:37.510
So tomorrow we're going to look at a clip
of Dr. Jill Biden handling a sort of bogus

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:39.959
direction during a CNN interview.

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:42.519
But Joe Biden doing the right thing here.

00:03:42.519 --> 00:03:46.599
Joe Biden is correctly identifying that you
can't win with that question.

00:03:46.599 --> 00:03:51.379
If Joe Biden says, yes, I will consider packing
the court or I will definitely try to pack

00:03:51.379 --> 00:03:57.129
the court, the right goes crazy and calls
Biden an authoritarian and a fascist and all

00:03:57.129 --> 00:03:59.749
the things that Donald Trump actually wants
to be.

00:03:59.749 --> 00:04:03.279
If Joe Biden says, yes, I will pack the court.

00:04:03.279 --> 00:04:07.609
Those on the left who think it's a bad idea,
that it's a divisive idea.

00:04:07.609 --> 00:04:09.310
They will get mad at Joe Biden.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:12.419
And then if Joe Biden says, no, I won't consider
packing the court.

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:17.139
Those on the left who want him to pack the
court will say this is why the Dems lose their

00:04:17.139 --> 00:04:18.139
week.

00:04:18.139 --> 00:04:20.919
They give then they won't ever do what they
need to do.

00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:27.069
So Joe Biden correctly points out right now
Donald Trump is trying to get Amy CONI Barrett

00:04:27.069 --> 00:04:28.099
confirmed.

00:04:28.099 --> 00:04:30.560
She wants to get rid of the Affordable Care
Act.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.970
She's very much against Roe v. Wade.

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:33.970
Period.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:35.479
That's the issue right now.

00:04:35.479 --> 00:04:41.210
And this is something that I guess we've become
kind of dissents or not these that we've we've

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:48.530
I am Reeth sensitized to when an elected official
properly handles a bad question or a poorly

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:54.669
framed question, because with the Trump administration,
it's either Trump's ask the question and he

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:57.020
just talks about something totally different.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:00.419
Or Trump is asked a question and he lies.

00:05:00.419 --> 00:05:05.280
But this is actually how you handle some of
these questions that have no possible upside.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:09.600
Now, earlier in the event, Joe Biden also
made it very clear, and I think that this

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:15.250
goes to something that's astute that Biden
and his campaign are doing right now.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:20.789
Joe Biden makes clear that what Donald Trump
is doing on the Supreme Court is outrageous

00:05:20.789 --> 00:05:25.860
and that at the core of it is wanting to dismantle
a lot of this policy, including the Affordable

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:26.860
Care Act.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:27.860
Take a look.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:34.009
Surely before Justice Ginsburg's passed, she
she told her granddaughter, and I quote, My

00:05:34.009 --> 00:05:40.600
most fervent wish is that I will not be replaced
until a new president is installed.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:45.300
And the quote wasn't a personal request.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:48.430
Wasn't a favor being asked for.

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:55.240
It was the last act of a long, unflinching
career of standing up for American democracy.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:06:02.560
Never before in our nation's history as a
Supreme Court justice been nominated and installed

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:08.129
while a presidential election is already underway.

00:06:08.129 --> 00:06:16.229
It defies every precedent, every expectation
of a nation where the people, the people are

00:06:16.229 --> 00:06:19.810
sovereign and the rule of law reigns.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:27.080
But yesterday, before Justice Ginsburg could
be laid to rest and after one hundred thousands

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:33.750
of Americans had already cast their ballots,
the president nominated a successor to her

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.540
seat.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:39.190
It's no mystery about what's happening here.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.580
President Trump was trying to throw out the
Affordable Care Act.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:46.150
He's been trying to do it for the last four
years.

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:52.610
The Republican Party has been trying to eliminate
it for a decade.

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:55.909
So I don't agree with Biden all the time on
policy.

00:06:55.909 --> 00:06:58.650
I certainly don't agree with Biden all the
time on strategy.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.229
But I think that this is logical.

00:07:00.229 --> 00:07:04.740
Keep the pressure on what they are trying
to do right now rather than the hypotheticals.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:08.580
If Joe Biden wins, there's more than enough
time for those hypotheticals.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:13.310
And when the hypotheticals might ingratiate
you with some but alienate others, there's

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:15.860
very little upside to going in that direction.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:21.949
What Joe Biden is trying to do here is to
cement in the minds of the voters the stakes

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:27.289
that are at play and that hopefully I'm hoping
he will do that tomorrow night during the

00:07:27.289 --> 00:07:30.249
first presidential debate tomorrow, Tuesday.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:36.110
We will be starting live coverage of the first
presidential debate between Donald Trump and

00:07:36.110 --> 00:07:43.159
Joseph R. Biden Jr. eight thirty p.m. Eastern
Time, five thirty p.m. Pacific.

00:07:43.159 --> 00:07:47.189
We will be live on YouTube, live on Twitch
and live on Facebook.

00:07:47.189 --> 00:07:49.360
I hope you will join me.

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:52.509
This is precisely the correct messaging from
Joe Biden.

00:07:52.509 --> 00:07:58.430
And by the way, as of now, we're getting into
just real nitty gritty policy.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:02.639
I still don't understand how repealing or
gutting the Affordable Care Act without a

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:07.110
real replacement plan, which Trump doesn't
have days before an election.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:11.530
I don't even get how that's a winning strategy
for Donald Trump.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.210
That's another story altogether.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:17.580
But they are again talking about how quickly
can we get rid of the Affordable Care Act

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.909
days before an election with no plan to replace
it.

00:08:20.909 --> 00:08:22.259
You're going to try to get rid of it.

00:08:22.259 --> 00:08:25.080
I don't see how that's winning electoral strategy.

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:28.080
But Donald Trump did win in 2016, so maybe
he knows something I don't.

